* TOOL_BACKUPS
* Backups and restores on one screen: the saved backup directory, the archives in it with what each holds, who is signed on (a backup and a restore both need everyone else out), and
* BACKUP.ACCOUNT, RESTORE.ACCOUNT and SET.BACKUP.DIRECTORY behind a box (S.75, plan .claude/plan-fullscreen-toolkit.md section 5, A8).
* Copyright (c) 2026, SD Core for Linux.  This program is free software; you can redistribute
* it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later.
*
* START-HISTORY:
* 10 Nov 26 Windows port - from Linux e3490a7f; two box texts no longer say "the root helper": SDSYS packs and saves BACKUPDIR itself here, elevated.
* 28 Oct 26 dm  S.88 L2: the three boxes are panes of the layout service ($tk_layout): drawn exactly as before at 140 by 43, and in a larger window the archive list takes the extra rows,
*               every box and text is as wide as the window, and the manifest lists as many accounts as the box has rows. The rows, widths, hit tests and the [?] button are counted from the
*               pane rectangles; the "... and N more accounts" line stands on the box's last row and counts from the rows the box has (8 accounts fit at 140 by 43).
* 25 Oct 26 dm  New.
* 1 Nov 26 dm  S.97 stage 2 (group B): the AI line ($tk_aipage), as tool.voc has it: F6 or AI > Ask the AI; refresh is the one action offered to the model.
* 8 Nov 26 dm  S.176: F6 / Shift-F6 are the box keys of every page ($tk_aipage 'ring'): from the list to the AI line and back; AI > Ask the AI is a menu entry of its own.
* 8 Nov 26 dm  S.179: Ctrl-T the theme (View > Theme) and Ctrl-K the keys of the page (Help > Keys), through $tk_std as on every page.
* 9 Nov 26 dm  S.186: View > Mouse and Ctrl-O (the log of the commands run), the same on every page (the cases act:std.mouse and ctrl-o, through $tk_std).
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   TOOL.BACKUPS      (SDSYS's VOC only; the audience is the administrator, asked of the kernel before anything is read)
*
*   A full-screen page, in the toolkit's frame (140 columns by 43 lines at least).  The top box names the saved backup directory (SET.BACKUP.DIRECTORY's, read through !acc_os_bakdir),
*   says how many archives it holds, and says whether anyone else is signed on: BACKUP.ACCOUNT and RESTORE.ACCOUNT both run only when every other session has logged out, and LOGIN refuses
*   new ones while either runs, so the page lists the other sessions (!acc_hold CHECK) and says plainly that the keys will be refused while they are there.  The list is the archives of the
*   directory (the files SD-host-accounts-yyyymmdd-hhmmss.zip): when it was made, by which computer, for how many accounts and how large.  The box at the foot shows the manifest of the one
*   under the cursor, read without unpacking anything (!acc_archive MANIFEST): the product, the SD version, the host, and each account with its files, bytes and directories.
*
*   WHAT IT RUNS.  Four commands, each through the box that shows the sentence and what it does, answered Run or Cancel (Cancel is what Enter chooses), and run through $tk_runx, which allows
*   only the four first words below; the verbs ask for the administrator themselves and write their own audit lines:
*     B   BACKUP.ACCOUNT ALL                       every account to the saved directory
*     A   BACKUP.ACCOUNT name [name ...]            the accounts you name (a question asks for the names; each must be a plain account name)
*     R   RESTORE.ACCOUNT archive ALL NO.QUERY      the archive under the cursor, EVERY account it holds, replacing the accounts of those names (the box lists them, from the manifest, and
*                                                  needs the word RESTORE typed; NO.QUERY is given because the box has asked and the verb's own question cannot be answered through here)
*     D   SET.BACKUP.DIRECTORY path                 the directory backups go to (a question asks for the path; the verb proves it writable and saves it)
*   It never runs one while another session is signed on (it says so instead of showing the box).  A backup and a restore need root for the packing and the placing; the page cannot make
*   them work where they cannot, and shows the verb's own words when it does not.
*
*   Keys: Up, Down, PgUp, PgDn, Home, End; B, A, R, D as above; F5 reads the directory, the archives and the sessions again; F1 or ? or a click on the [?] explains the page; Ctrl-Q leaves.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
program $tool_backups
$catalog $tool_backups

$include keys.h
$include int$keys.h
$include err.h
$include sl.h
$include tk.h
$include accbak.h

   prompt ''

   allow = 'backup.account restore.account set.backup.directory'   ;* the commands this page may run
   call $tk_open('tool.backups', 'admin', ctx, err)
   if err # '' then
      display err
      stop
   end
   void kernel(K$AUDIT, 'tool start app=tool.backups')

   keys = ''
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f1', 'help', 'help', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'b', 'backup all', 'backupall', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'a', 'backup some', 'backupsome', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'r', 'restore', 'restore', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'd', 'directory', 'directory', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f5', 'read', 'refresh', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'ctrl-q', 'quit', 'quit', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'esc', 'menu', 'menu', '', 1)                ;* S.88 U3: Esc opens the menu bar (this page holds nothing of its own that Esc closes first)
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'quit', '&File', '&Quit', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'backupall', '&Backups', '&Back up all accounts', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'backupsome', '&Backups', 'Back up &some accounts', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'restore', '&Backups', '&Restore the archive', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'directory', '&Backups', '&Directory of the archives', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'refresh', '&View', '&Refresh', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'help', '&Help', '&Help on this page', '', '')
   call $tk_std('keys', ctx, keys, '', '')                ;* S.179: Ctrl-T theme, Ctrl-K keys and their View and Help entries, as on every page
   * S.97 stage 2 (group B): the AI line.  The page offers the AI only refresh (an administrator's page: a backup, a restore and the directory are not offered without the
   * owner's word); a proposal is carried out by the page's own key.  Where the AI is not usable nothing here adds a key, a row or a line.
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'refresh', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_aipage('init', ctx, keys, '', '', aout)

   gosub lay.declare                                            ;* the panes; VA (the archive rows on the screen) and DV (the manifest rows) come from them
   ha = fmt('Made', '21L') : fmt('Size', '12R') : '  ' : fmt('Accounts', '9L') : fmt('Product', '12L') : 'File'

   bdir = '' ; bderr = '' ; nark = 0 ; others = '' ; hold.err = ''
   anm = '' ; asize = '' ; awhen = '' ; aacc = '' ; aprod = ''
   ci = 1 ; ta = 0
   gen = 0
   done = 0
   msg = ''

   gosub read.all
   gosub draw.all

   loop
      call $tk_menubar('draw', ctx, keys, 'Backups', '', '', mr)            ;* the bar first: it writes row 0 whole, and the frame then writes the app name at its right end
      call $tk_frame(ctx, keys, 'Backups', msg)
      call $sl_curat(0, ctx<TK.C.YSTAT>)
      nm = ''
      screen key returning nm
      mr = ''
      ao = ''
      if nm # '' then call $tk_aipage('key', ctx, keys, 'Backups', nm, ao)           ;* S.97 stage 2: while the AI line has the focus it takes the keys, before the bar sees them
      if ao<1> = 'replay' then nm = ao<2>                                            ;* an action the AI proposed and the person accepted: this page's own key for it
      if ao<1> # '' then msg = ao<4>
      if nm # '' and ao<1> = '' then call $tk_menubar('key', ctx, keys, 'Backups', nm, 0, mr)       ;* F10, Alt and a letter, and Esc (nothing of this page's is open): the bar
      if mr<1> # '' then nm = mr<4>
      begin case
         case ao<1> = 'taken'
            if ao<3> then
               gen += 1                                                               ;* the preview, the wait and the answer covered the page: all of it is drawn again
               ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
               gosub draw.all
            end
         case nm = ''
            if status() = ER$EOF then exit
         case nm = 'guardquit'
            exit
         case nm = 'resize'
            call $tk_layout('refresh', ctx, '', lay.chg)
            gosub lay.get
            gen += 1
            ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
            gosub draw.all
         case nm = 'mouse'
            gosub on.mouse
         case 1
            gosub on.key
      end case
      if done then exit
   repeat

   call $tk_close(ctx)
   stop

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- what the machine says

* The saved directory, its archives (newest first), the manifest facts of each, and who else is signed on; the cursor goes back to the archive it was on
read.all:
   sel.a = ''
   if nark > 0 and ci >= 1 and ci <= nark then sel.a = anm<ci>
   call !acc_os_bakdir('GET', bdir, bderr)
   anm = '' ; asize = '' ; awhen = '' ; aacc = '' ; aprod = '' ; nark = 0
   if bderr = '' and bdir # '' then
      if ospath(bdir, OS$EXISTS) then gosub read.archives
   end
   call !acc_hold(ACCBAK$CHECK, others, hold.err)
   if ci > nark then ci = nark
   if ci < 1 then ci = 1
   if sel.a # '' then
      for i = 1 to nark
         if anm<i> = sel.a then
            ci = i
            exit
         end
      next i
   end
   return

* Every SD-*.zip of the directory, newest first by the time in its name; for each its size, when it was made, and the manifest's product, host and account count
read.archives:
   openpath bdir to df else return
   select df to 9
   names = ''
   loop
      readnext nm from 9 else exit
      if nm[1, 3] = 'SD-' and nm[len(nm) - 3, 4] = '.zip' and len(nm) > 20 then names<-1> = nm
   repeat
   close df
   if names = '' then return
   stamps = '' ; byname = ''
   for i = 1 to dcount(names, @fm)
      nm = names<i>
      st = nm[len(nm) - 18, 15]
      locate st in stamps<1> by 'DL' setting p else null
      ins st before stamps<p>
      ins nm before byname<p>
   next i
   for i = 1 to dcount(byname, @fm)
      nm = byname<i>
      stamp = stamps<i>
      nark += 1
      anm<nark> = nm
      info = ospath(bdir : @ds : nm, OS$INFO)
      asize<nark> = info<6>
      awhen<nark> = stamp[1, 4] : '-' : stamp[5, 2] : '-' : stamp[7, 2] : ' ' : stamp[10, 2] : ':' : stamp[12, 2] : ':' : stamp[14, 2]
      call !acc_archive('MANIFEST', bdir : @ds : nm, '', mtext, merr)
      aacc<nark> = '?' ; aprod<nark> = '?'
      if merr = '' then
         for l = 1 to dcount(mtext, @fm)
            ml = mtext<l>
            if ml[1, 10] = 'accounts: ' then aacc<nark> = ml[11, 20]
            if ml[1, 9] = 'product: ' then aprod<nark> = ml[10, 40]
         next l
      end
   next i
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the layout (S.88 L2)

* The page's three boxes as panes of $tk_layout: each size is the box drawn at 140 by 43 (the body is 138 by 39), so at that size nothing moves; in a larger window the archive list
* stretches (a table shows more rows) and every pane is as wide as the body.
lay.declare:
   d = ''
   d<1> = 'top' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 6 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   d<2> = 'list' : @vm : 2 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 20 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   d<3> = 'detail' : @vm : 3 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 13 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   call $tk_layout('declare', ctx, d, lay.err)
   gosub lay.get
   return

* The rectangles of the three panes, and what is counted from them: tw the width of a text line inside a box (134 at 140 by 43), VA the archive rows, DV the manifest rows
lay.get:
   lay.id = 'top'
   gosub lay.rect
   top.x = lay.x ; top.y = lay.y ; top.w = lay.w ; top.h = lay.h
   lay.id = 'list'
   gosub lay.rect
   lst.x = lay.x ; lst.y = lay.y ; lst.w = lay.w ; lst.h = lay.h
   lay.id = 'detail'
   gosub lay.rect
   det.x = lay.x ; det.y = lay.y ; det.w = lay.w ; det.h = lay.h
   body.y = ctx<TK.C.YBODY>
   tx = lst.x + 2
   tw = lst.w - 4
   mk.x = top.x + top.w - 5                                     ;* the [?] button, at the right end of the first row of the top box
   mk.y = top.y + 1
   VA = lst.h - 3
   DV = det.h - 2
   return

lay.rect:
   call $tk_layout('pane', ctx, lay.id, lay.r)
   lay.x = lay.r<1, 1>
   lay.y = lay.r<1, 2>
   lay.w = lay.r<1, 3>
   lay.h = lay.r<1, 4>
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- drawing

draw.all:
   cw2 = ctx<TK.C.W>
   chh = ctx<TK.C.H> - 5
   screen clear at 0,body.y size cw2,chh
   screen box at top.x,top.y size top.w,top.h title 'Backups'
   screen box at lst.x,lst.y size lst.w,lst.h title 'Archives'
   screen box at det.x,det.y size det.w,det.h title 'The archive under the cursor'
   gosub draw.top
   gosub redraw
   return

draw.top:
   if bderr # '' then
      s = 'The saved backup directory could not be read.'
   end else
      if bdir = '' then
         s = 'No backup directory has been saved. D saves one (SET.BACKUP.DIRECTORY).'
      end else
         s = 'Directory: ' : bdir : '   Archives: ' : nark
      end
   end
   screen text s[1, tw - 6] at tx,top.y + 1 attr 'bold' width tw - 6                  ;* 6 less than the other lines so that the [?] is clear
   no = dcount(others, @fm)
   if hold.err = '' or no = 0 then
      s = 'No other session is signed on: a backup or a restore can start.'
   end else
      s = no : ' other session' : (if no = 1 then ' is' else 's are') : ' signed on, so B, A and R are refused until they log out:'
      for k = 1 to no
         if k <= 4 then s := ' ' : others<k, 2> : ' (user ' : others<k, 1> : ')'
      next k
      if no > 4 then s := ' ...'
   end
   screen text s[1, tw] at tx,top.y + 2 width tw
   screen text 'A backup and a restore both run only when every other session has logged out, and LOGIN refuses new ones while they run.' at tx,top.y + 3 width tw
   screen text 'B backs every account up   A some   R restores the archive under the cursor   D sets the directory   F5 reads again' at tx,top.y + 4 width tw
   call $tk_help('mark', mk.x, mk.y, 0, 0)
   return

redraw:
   gosub draw.list
   gosub draw.detail
   return

draw.list:
   screen text ha at tx,lst.y + 1 attr 'header' width tw
   if ci <= ta then ta = ci - 1
   if ci > ta + VA then ta = ci - VA
   if ta < 0 then ta = 0
   for r = 1 to VA
      kk = ta + r
      s = ''
      if kk <= nark then
         s = fmt(awhen<kk>, '21L') : fmt(asize<kk>, '12R') : '  ' : fmt(aacc<kk>[1, 8], '9L') : fmt(aprod<kk>[1, 11], '12L') : anm<kk>
      end
      rat = 'normal'
      if kk = ci and kk <= nark then rat = 'highlight'
      screen text s[1, tw] at tx,lst.y + 1 + r attr rat width tw
   next r
   return

* The manifest of the archive under the cursor, one line each: the facts, then the accounts with their counts
draw.detail:
   for r = 1 to DV
      screen text '' at tx,det.y + r width tw
   next r
   if nark = 0 or ci < 1 or ci > nark then
      s = (if bdir = '' then 'There is no directory to look in.' else 'The directory holds no archive.')
      screen text s at tx,det.y + 1 width tw
      return
   end
   call !acc_archive('MANIFEST', bdir : @ds : anm<ci>, '', mtext, merr)
   if merr # '' then
      s = 'The manifest of this archive cannot be read: ' : merr<1, 1>
      screen text s at tx,det.y + 1 width tw
      return
   end
   lines = ''
   facts = ''
   accts = ''
   ac.f = '' ; ac.b = '' ; ac.d = ''
   cur = ''
   na = 0
   for l = 1 to dcount(mtext, @fm)
      ml = mtext<l>
      if ml[1, 9] = '[account ' then
         cur = ml[10, len(ml) - 10]
         na += 1
         accts<na> = cur
      end else
         if cur = '' then
            if ml # '' then facts<-1> = ml
         end else
            if ml[1, 7] = 'files: ' then ac.f<na> = ml[8, 20]
            if ml[1, 7] = 'bytes: ' then ac.b<na> = ml[8, 20]
            if ml[1, 6] = 'dirs: ' then ac.d<na> = ml[7, 20]
         end
      end
   next l
   s = ''
   for k = 1 to dcount(facts, @fm)
      ft = facts<k>
      if ft[1, 8] # 'format: ' and ft[1, 8] # 'accounts' then s := (if s = '' then '' else '   ') : ft
   next k
   lines<-1> = s
   lines<-1> = ''
   lines<-1> = fmt('Account', '28L') : fmt('Files', '10R') : fmt('Bytes', '16R') : fmt('Directories', '14R')
   for k = 1 to dcount(accts, @fm)
      lines<-1> = fmt(accts<k>[1, 27], '28L') : fmt(ac.f<k>, '10R') : fmt(ac.b<k>, '16R') : fmt(ac.d<k>, '14R')
   next k
   for r = 1 to dcount(lines, @fm)
      if r <= DV then
         lr = lines<r>
         screen text lr[1, tw] at tx,det.y + r width tw
      end
   next r
   if dcount(lines, @fm) > DV then
      s = '... and ' : na - (DV - 4) : ' more accounts'                ;* three lines (the facts, a blank, the heading) come before the accounts, and this line stands on the last row, in place of one
      screen text s at tx,det.y + DV width tw
   end
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- keys and mouse

on.key:
   msg = ''
   if len(nm) = 1 and nm >= 'A' and nm <= 'Z' then nm = downcase(nm)
   begin case
      case nm = 'up'
         if ci > 1 then ci -= 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'down'
         if ci < nark then ci += 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'pgup'
         ci -= VA
         if ci < 1 then ci = 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'pgdn'
         ci += VA
         if ci > nark then ci = nark
         if ci < 1 then ci = 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'home'
         ci = 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'end'
         ci = nark
         if ci < 1 then ci = 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'b'
         gosub do.backup.all
      case nm = 'a'
         gosub do.backup.some
      case nm = 'r'
         gosub do.restore
      case nm = 'd'
         gosub do.directory
      case nm = 'ctrl-t'                    ;* S.179: the theme, kept for the person - the same on every page ($tk_std)
         call $tk_std('theme', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
         if std.r<1> then gosub draw.all
         msg = std.r<2>
      case nm = 'act:std.mouse'             ;* S.186: View > Mouse, the same on every page ($tk_std)
         call $tk_std('mouse', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
         msg = std.r<2>
      case nm = 'ctrl-o'                    ;* S.186: the log of the commands this page ran (View > Output; $tk_std)
         call $tk_std('output', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
      case nm = 'ctrl-k'                    ;* S.179: the keys of this page, in a box
         call $tk_std('keylist', ctx, keys, 'Backups', std.r)
      case nm = 'f5'
         gosub read.all
         gosub draw.all
         msg = 'read again'
      case nm = 'f1' or nm = '?'
         call $tk_help('box', 'tool.backups.page', hm, 0, 0)
         if hm # '' then msg = hm
      case nm = 'f6' or nm = 'shift-f6' or nm = 'act:ai'
         call $tk_aipage('ring', ctx, keys, 1, nm : @fm : 1, ap)            ;* S.176: F6 / Shift-F6 go round the boxes (one here) and the AI line; AI > Ask the AI goes to the line
         msg = ap<2>
      case nm = 'ctrl-q'
         done = 1
   end case
   return

on.mouse:
   screen mouse returning mev else mev = ''
   if mev = '' then return
   mr = ''
   call $tk_menubar('click', ctx, keys, 'Backups', mev, '', mr)                   ;* a click on the bar on row 0
   if mr<1> # '' then
      nm = mr<4>
      if nm # '' then gosub on.key                          ;* a bar left with nothing chosen has no name: the status message stays
      return
   end
   call $tk_aipage('mouse', ctx, keys, 'Backups', mev, ap)                          ;* S.97 stage 2: a click on the AI line gives it the focus
   if ap # '' then
      msg = ap
      return
   end
   call $tk_help('hit', mev, mk.x, mk.y, hit.m)
   if hit.m then
      call $tk_help('box', 'tool.backups.page', hm, 0, 0)
      if hm # '' then msg = hm
      return
   end
   if mev<1> = 'press' and mev<2> = 1 then
      mx = mev<3>
      my = mev<4>
      if mx >= tx and mx <= tx + tw - 1 and my >= lst.y + 2 and my <= lst.y + 1 + VA then
         if ta + my - (lst.y + 1) <= nark then
            ci = ta + my - (lst.y + 1)
            gosub redraw
         end
      end
   end
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the commands

* sent and el are the sentence and its explanation, typed is null or the word to type; the box is shown, the command run when Run was chosen, everything read again, and the verb's words shown
confirm.and.run:
   call $tk_confirm(sent, el, typed, res, cmsg)
   if res = 'run' then
      call $tk_runx(allow, sent, out, stat, err)
      gosub read.all
      gosub draw.all
      if err # '' then
         msg = err
      end else
         msg = sent[1, 60] : ' ran (status ' : stat : ')'
         lastl = ''
         for k = 1 to dcount(out, @fm)
            if trim(out<k>) # '' then lastl = trim(out<k>)
         next k
         if lastl # '' then msg = msg : ': ' : lastl
      end
   end else
      msg = cmsg
   end
   return

* The other sessions must be gone: if any are left say so (the verb would refuse too) and show no box.  others_ok is 1 when the page may go on.
check.alone:
   others_ok = 1
   call !acc_hold(ACCBAK$CHECK, others, hold.err)
   if hold.err # '' and dcount(others, @fm) > 0 then
      others_ok = 0
      msg = dcount(others, @fm) : ' other session(s) are signed on; the verb would refuse until they log out'
      gosub draw.top
   end
   return

do.backup.all:
   gosub check.alone
   if not(others_ok) then return
   if bdir = '' then
      msg = 'no backup directory has been saved: D saves one first'
      return
   end
   sent = 'backup.account all'
   typed = ''
   el = ''
   el<-1> = 'Every account is packed into one archive in ' : bdir : ', named SD-host-all-date-time.zip. SDSYS is not backed up and no password or credential is in it.'
   el<-1> = 'Everyone else must be logged out, and LOGIN refuses new sessions while it runs. The packing is done by SDSYS, which runs elevated.'
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

do.backup.some:
   gosub check.alone
   if not(others_ok) then return
   if bdir = '' then
      msg = 'no backup directory has been saved: D saves one first'
      return
   end
   screen ask 'Accounts to back up: names separated by spaces' width 80 value '' title 'Backup some accounts' returning names.in else return
   names.in = trim(names.in)
   if names.in = '' then return
   good = 'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789._-'
   ok = 1
   for w = 1 to dcount(names.in, ' ')
      wd = field(names.in, ' ', w)
      for q = 1 to len(wd)
         if index(good, wd[q, 1], 1) = 0 then ok = 0
      next q
   next w
   if not(ok) or dcount(names.in, ' ') > 20 then
      msg = 'an account name has only a-z, 0-9, dot, dash and underscore; up to 20 names'
      return
   end
   sent = 'backup.account ' : names.in
   typed = ''
   el = ''
   el<-1> = 'The accounts named are packed into one archive in ' : bdir : '. A name that is not an account is refused by the verb before anything is written.'
   el<-1> = 'Everyone else must be logged out, and LOGIN refuses new sessions while it runs.'
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

* The archive under the cursor, every account it holds; the box lists the accounts from its manifest and wants RESTORE typed
do.restore:
   gosub check.alone
   if not(others_ok) then return
   if nark = 0 or ci < 1 or ci > nark then
      msg = 'there is no archive to restore'
      return
   end
   call !acc_archive('MANIFEST', bdir : @ds : anm<ci>, '', mtext, merr)
   if merr # '' then
      msg = 'the manifest of this archive cannot be read'
      return
   end
   accts = ''
   for l = 1 to dcount(mtext, @fm)
      ml = mtext<l>
      if ml[1, 9] = '[account ' then accts<-1> = ml[10, len(ml) - 10]
   next l
   * a restore that would MAKE an account asks for its password, which cannot be typed through a page: every account of the archive must be registered here already
   openpath @sdsys : @ds : 'accounts' to reg.f else
      msg = 'the account register cannot be read'
      return
   end
   select reg.f to 9
   regids = ''
   loop
      readnext rid from 9 else exit
      regids<-1> = rid
   repeat
   close reg.f
   missing = ''
   for k = 1 to dcount(accts, @fm)
      if index(@fm : regids : @fm, @fm : accts<k> : @fm, 1) = 0 then missing<-1> = accts<k>
   next k
   if missing # '' then
      msg = 'the archive holds accounts that are not registered here (' : convert(@fm, ' ', missing) : '): restore it at the prompt, where a new account can be given its password'
      return
   end
   sent = 'restore.account ' : anm<ci> : ' all no.query'
   typed = 'RESTORE'
   el = ''
   el<-1> = 'EVERY account in this archive replaces the account of the same name: ' : convert(@fm, ' ', accts) : '.'
   el<-1> = 'What an account holds now is lost. The archive is unpacked and checked against its manifest before anything is changed.'
   el<-1> = 'Everyone else must be logged out, and LOGIN refuses new sessions while it runs. no.query is given because this box has asked.'
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

do.directory:
   cv = bdir
   screen ask 'Backup directory: an absolute path (it is made if it can be, and proved writable)' width 100 value cv title 'Backup directory' returning nd else return
   nd = trim(nd)
   if nd = '' or nd[1, 1] # '/' or len(nd) > 200 or index(nd, ' ', 1) > 0 then
      msg = 'give an absolute path with no space in it'
      return
   end
   sent = 'set.backup.directory ' : nd
   typed = ''
   el = ''
   el<-1> = 'Backups and restores will use this directory from now on. The verb makes it if it can, proves SDSYS can put a file in it, and saves the one line BACKUPDIR in sd.conf.'
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

end

